    "rating": 4.4,
    "reference": "ChIJW7M5FTY2yUwRd6l6TNcmlms",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Chris Hogan",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114401624728012512972/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUTi0L63CYGS5m5EPL_Jv0uj9gYFqeodrVomYle6bo5Ey5nn7Ck=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "4 months ago",
        "text": "We are shopping for my son's first bike and we have visited approximately 6 dealerships in the last month. Comptant Vaudreuil is by far the closest to us and they have our desired model in stock but after 3 seperate visits I have to say, I have never felt more like I was invisible than I have at this dealership.\n\nDuring our first visit, we were \"just looking\", we didn't really need any help and it was a good thing because not a single member of the staff approached us. A 2nd visit was to show my wife what we were targeting as a purchase. This time someone did approach us but it was to tell us that my son was not allowed to sit on the bike. We were told that we would need to speak with a salesman if we wanted to  check sizing of the bike for my son's comfort and height. When we asked if we could see a salesman, we were told that only one was available and he would be called up from downstairs. After 25-30 minutes we got fed up and left. On the way out, we saw 3 staff members chatting in one of the sales offices downstairs. Not a word to us as we walked by. We were not impressed.\n\nMy son wanted to look at another model of bike last night and Comptant had it in stock as well as the first bike of interest, so against my better judgement, we went back to give them another try. A young lady upstairs from the accessories and apparel department asked us if we needed and any help (first time that happened in 3 trips), we said \"yes, we would like to speak with a salesman\", she made a call and told us that one would be with us shortly. That took over 20 minutes as he stopped to help another customer on the way to us, despite his being called for us. When he did approach us, he apologized for the delay and we asked him about the pricing on the bike as it said \"see salesman for promotional details\". When we asked about the discount, the salesmen told us that he didn't know the details and he had to go downstairs but if we could take a picture of the bike and the stock number and bring it down, he would look into it. Again, REALLY not impressed. Shouldn't HE be the one taking the details? When we got downstairs, he sat us in his office where we waited ANOTHER 20 mins while he dealt with the other customer in another office and just when we were about to leave, he showed up. He took FOREVER to figure out what bike it was in the system and gave us a sale price that was the highest of any we have encountered so far. When I brought that up, he explained to me that, while that might be true, Comptant is known for the 1st rate customer service. I was stunned at that response, talk about deflection. Based on my 3 visits, that would not be how I would describe Comptant's service. He never revisted pricing or made any attempts to do any better, even when I stated again that some other dealerships were coming in lower than what he was offering.\n\nBottom line, I find the salesman was deeply lacking in knowledge of the 2 bikes that we inquired about in the brief time that he spent with us upstairs, we felt invisible and unimportant as potential buyers. Pricing is higher than a number of other dealerships and we felt zero confidence that buying from this dealership would be a good transaction based on what we had experienced to this point.\n\nOur interactions with sales staff in numerous other dealerships has been FAR superior to this one and we now know we will be making a farther trip to another dealership that welcomed us, helped us and followed up with us on our visits. They offered better service, better pricing and better overall experience than that at Comptant.\n\nI don't see us ever walking into Comptant again.",
        "time": 1760032534,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Steve Joly",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116407957160369025431/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIwuKKlayF_rlrJw2Mj6qpWVn5rYgRHGo2XlQL9uqV4FEx4zg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "3 years ago",
        "text": "The worse service I have ever had.  Ordered a KTM Super Duke 1290 R EVO and I have to constantly go there to get information, this is 2 weeks after delivery date, which was NEVER delivered.  Damaged in \"Crate\" sent to paint shop who cannot get it painted.  Over a dozen messages left for salesman \"Nicolas Prevost\" whereas I continuously have to personally drive there and get information.  So fast to take deposit without any care for the customer satisfaction.  The minimal task of keeping the client up to date with latest information is not even done.  So simple to blame COVID on lack of staff, etc..... but when a client pays 24k for a new bike and gets constant run around is not a way to run a business.  I would never, I repeat NEVER recommend this dealership to anyone.  Please do your due diligence before even stepping foot in this establishment.  If not buyer beware.  Utterly atrocious this lack of professionalism from this business.\n\nWould NOT recommend",
        "time": 1666291828,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "brion kelly",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108112798476060461197/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVOOr6tIQEk1NVPjCac8tkJv_RwXAkZcDy3OuJng0HS6fxWCsnr=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "6 years ago",
        "text": "Great help from Phillip  and others in the parts dept... Also  Martin Dupuis is always very helpful . I hope my experience in service dept goes as well",
        "time": 1573321401,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Proprio",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102391720495154635944/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUMLSJx9_bPPW5d8MAN4-oboM8_fmn5Vz44WcGyV2PFKn-yUKBR=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 2,
        "relative_time_description": "2 years ago",
        "text": "Contant did the 100hr inspection on my SeaDoo. After that, the PWC was not driving properly. The first thing I did was test the oil level. Bingo! There was too much oil - way too much oil. The service department said it’s not possible and were completely unhelpful in finding a solution. Now I have to purchase an oil extractor to fix their mess.",
        "time": 1687794991,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Denis Lecuyer",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117461656614424774199/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVxS22Hz0TNN_QXKUxBPN1bkDBMCS87_7d92-TgjLr1J01qvx9E=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
